# What `npm run format` may never rewrite.
#
# `format` is `prettier --write .` — it WRITES. Until this file existed nothing
# recorded which paths that was allowed to touch, and a plain run would have
# rewritten pnpm-lock.yaml and every drizzle/meta snapshot (measured 2026-11-27).
# A formatter is safe on source and dangerous on anything a tool compares
# byte-for-byte, so the generated and authoritative files are named here.

# Dependency and build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
*.log

# Lockfiles: a formatter must never touch dependency resolution.
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Drizzle's migration journal and snapshots. drizzle-kit compares these to decide
# what a migration already contains; they are machine-written and must stay as
# drizzle-kit wrote them.
drizzle/meta/

# Applied as a dependency patch by pnpm. Its bytes must match the published
# tarball or the patch stops applying.
patches/

# Written by the host runtime, not by hand.
client/public/__manus__/

# CI definitions. Prettier's YAML printer reflows `run:` scalars, and a reflowed
# shell script is a different shell script.
.github/workflows/

# Per-file provenance, written by tools/manifest.py. Reformatting it would drift
# every recorded blob sha.
MANIFEST.json
